But how do we efficiently get the next maximum each time? Because each row is being modified by removing the maximum each time. So for each row, we can sort it in descending order, and then for each step, take the first element, then the second, etc. Because once you sort each row in descending order, the first element is the first max, then the second is the next max, etc. So for each row, after sorting, the elements are in order of their removal.

So the approach would be:

